1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:05,622
VitalOrbit. An autonomous onboard health system for deep-space crews.

2
00:00:05,622 --> 00:00:08,771
When Earth is nineteen light-minutes away,

3
00:00:08,771 --> 00:00:11,470
the crew is its own first responder.

4
00:00:11,970 --> 00:00:15,347
On Mars, help can't be forty minutes away.

5
00:00:15,347 --> 00:00:19,689
One-way signal delay runs four to twenty-four minutes,

6
00:00:19,689 --> 00:00:24,754
and during solar conjunction the link disappears for two weeks.

7
00:00:24,754 --> 00:00:26,845
NASA's five RIDGE hazards:

8
00:00:26,845 --> 00:00:31,750
radiation, isolation, distance, gravity, hostile environment,

9
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:35,288
do slow damage nobody on Earth sees in time.

10
00:00:35,788 --> 00:00:40,078
So we built one system that detects, guides, and remembers.

11
00:00:40,078 --> 00:00:43,278
A personal anomaly model for each astronaut,

12
00:00:43,278 --> 00:00:45,823
trained on their own wearable data.

13
00:00:45,823 --> 00:00:49,895
Long-mission risk forecasting to the end of the mission.

14
00:00:49,895 --> 00:00:53,167
And an offline assistant with smart pharmacy:

15
00:00:53,167 --> 00:00:56,730
guided first aid, with timers, voice, and Arabic.

16
00:00:57,230 --> 00:01:01,025
It works as one chain. Vitals from real wearable data.

17
00:01:01,025 --> 00:01:05,943
A personal model watching for deviation from that person's own rhythm.

18
00:01:05,943 --> 00:01:08,332
A check-in that asks how you feel.

19
00:01:08,332 --> 00:01:11,916
The assistant, with protocol, timers, and pharmacy.

20
00:01:11,916 --> 00:01:14,375
And Earth, nineteen minutes behind,

21
00:01:14,375 --> 00:01:17,607
with a structured SOAP report already written.

22
00:01:18,107 --> 00:01:23,199
Does it work? Three thousand four hundred fifty-six real readings from four

23
00:01:23,199 --> 00:01:25,983
people, plus twelve injected emergencies.

24
00:01:25,983 --> 00:01:30,192
Twelve of twelve detected, the correct vital named every time.

25
00:01:30,192 --> 00:01:35,216
Forty-five minutes median, to the first alert. Zero false critical alerts.

26
00:01:35,216 --> 00:01:39,630
And every number in the app is tagged: real, simulated, or model.

27
00:01:40,130 --> 00:01:44,826
Built for Mars, and useful wherever the doctor is far away.

28
00:01:44,826 --> 00:01:49,841
Antarctic stations, submarines, offshore rigs, remote villages,

29
00:01:49,841 --> 00:01:54,378
field hospitals. For crews, earlier warnings and privacy.

30
00:01:54,378 --> 00:01:57,562
For flight surgeons, structured reports,

31
00:01:57,562 --> 00:02:00,268
ready the moment the link returns.

32
00:02:00,768 --> 00:02:07,139
Code and run instructions are on GitHub at three A M U R R, VitalOrbit.

33
00:02:07,139 --> 00:02:10,728
Team CUPIQ, Egyptian Chinese University,

34
00:02:10,728 --> 00:02:14,317
built with help from Claude. VitalOrbit:

35
00:02:14,317 --> 00:02:17,008
medicine beyond Earth's reach.
